1. THE THREE PILLARS
--------------------
  Metrics  numbers over time (CPU, requests/s, error rate, latency)
           -> Prometheus, Grafana; cloud: CloudWatch, Azure Monitor,
              Google Cloud Monitoring, managed Prometheus
  Logs     text events from apps and components
           -> Fluent Bit/Vector/Alloy -> Loki, Elasticsearch/OpenSearch,
              CloudWatch Logs
  Traces   the path of one request across services
           -> OpenTelemetry -> Tempo, Jaeger, X-Ray
OpenTelemetry (OTel) is the standard for instrumenting all three.


2. PROMETHEUS IN 5 MINUTES
--------------------------
- PULL model: Prometheus scrapes http://target:port/metrics every N s.
- Time series: metric name + labels, e.g.
    http_requests_total{method="GET", code="200", pod="web-1"}
- Types: counter (only goes up), gauge (up/down), histogram, summary.
- PromQL examples:
    rate(http_requests_total[5m])                       per-second rate
    sum by (namespace) (rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total[5m]))
    container_memory_working_set_bytes{namespace="prod"}
    kube_deployment_status_replicas_available
    histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))
- Alerting rules -> Alertmanager -> Slack/email/PagerDuty.


3. WHERE KUBERNETES METRICS COME FROM
-------------------------------------
  node-exporter (DaemonSet)   node CPU, memory, disk, network
  kubelet / cAdvisor          per-container CPU/memory
  kube-state-metrics          object state: replicas, pod phase,
                              restarts, job status ...
  control plane endpoints     apiserver, scheduler, etcd metrics
  your app                    /metrics endpoint (client libraries)
(metrics-server is different: only for k top/HPA, not history.)


4. kube-prometheus-stack
------------------------
One Helm chart: Prometheus Operator + Prometheus + Alertmanager +
Grafana + node-exporter + kube-state-metrics + dashboards + alert
rules. The operator adds CRDs:
  ServiceMonitor / PodMonitor   "scrape these Services/pods"
  PrometheusRule                alerting/recording rules


5. WHAT TO ALERT ON
-------------------
Alert on SYMPTOMS users feel (error rate, latency, availability) and
on things that will soon break (disk filling, certificate expiring,
crash looping), not on every high CPU spike. The "golden signals":
latency, traffic, errors, saturation.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- Metrics, logs, traces; OpenTelemetry ties them together.
- Prometheus scrapes /metrics; PromQL queries; Alertmanager notifies.
- ServiceMonitor tells Prometheus what to scrape.
